"A 'Blob' is a data element that represents a file that is contained with its source code in the value attribute."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A File is a data element that represents an address to a file (a locator)."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A basic event element."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A capability is the implementation-independent description of the potential of an asset to achieve a certain effect in the physical or virtual world."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A data element is a submodel element that is not further composed out of other submodel elements."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A data element that represents an annotation that holds for the relationship between the two elements"@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A key is a reference to an element by its ID."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A pair of a value together with its global unique id."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A property is a data element that has a multi-language value."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A property is a data element that has a single value."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A qualifier is a type-value-pair that makes additional statements w.r.t. the value of the element."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A range data element is a data element that defines a range with min and max."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A reference element is a data element that defines a logical reference to another element within the same or another AAS or a reference to an external object or entity."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A relationship element is used to define a relationship between two elements being either referable (model reference) or external (global reference)."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A set of value reference pairs."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A specific asset ID describes a generic supplementary identifying attribute of the asset."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A submodel consists of zero or more submodel elements."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A submodel defines a specific aspect of the asset represented by the AAS."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A submodel element collection is a kind of struct, i.e. a a logical encapsulation of multiple named values. It has a fixed number of submodel elements."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A submodel element is an element suitable for the description and differentiation of assets."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A submodel element list is an ordered list of submodel elements."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"A value reference pair within a value list. Each value has a global unique id defining its semantic."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Actual content of the data specification"@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Additional domain-specific, typically proprietary identifier for the asset like e.g., serial number etc."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Additional qualification of a qualifiable element."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Administrative information of an identifiable element."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Administrative meta-information for an element like version information."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"An annotated relationship element is a relationship element that can be annotated with additional data elements."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"An asset administration shell."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"An element that has a globally unique identifier."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"An element that is referable by its 'idShort'."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"An element with a kind is an element that can either represent a template or an instance."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"An entity is a submodel element that is used to model entities."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"An event element."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"An extension of the element."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"An operation is a submodel element with input and output variables."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Asset administration shell"@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Bookmark or a similar local identifier of a subordinate part of a primary resource"@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Concept description"@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Concrete, clearly identifiable element instance. Its creation and validation may be guided by a corresponding element template."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Container for the sets of different identifiables."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Content of data specification template for concept descriptions for properties, values and value lists conformant to IEC 61360."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Content type of the content of the 'Blob'."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Data Type"@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Data element."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Data specification content is part of a data specification template and defines which additional attributes shall be added to the element instance that references the data specification template and meta information about the template itself."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Data type of the min und max"@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Data type of the qualifier value."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Data type of the value"@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Defines the necessary information of an event instance sent out or received."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Defines whether order in list is relevant. If 'orderRelevant' = False then the list is representing a set or a bag."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Definition in different languages"@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Denotes whether the Asset is of kind 'Type' or 'Instance'."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Denotes which kind of entity is referenced."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Describes an argument or result of an operation via a submodel element"@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Describes statements applicable to the entity by a set of submodel elements, typically with a qualified value."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Describes whether the entity is a co-managed entity or a self-managed entity."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Description or comments on the element."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Direction"@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Direction of event."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Display name. Can be provided in several languages."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Element that can be extended by proprietary extensions."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Element that can be extended by using data specification templates."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Element that can have a semantic definition plus some supplemental semantic definitions."@en a rdfs:Resource .

"Embed the content of a data specification."@en a rdfs:Resource .

